SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2026 by Marcelle Kress von Wendland, The Olamni Research Group and Bancstreet Capital Partners Ltd, London, UK
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

CENTRAL PACKAGE MANAGEMENT (CPM) — engineer ruling Q-shiras-36, 2026-09-01.
"Adopt CPM fleet-wide, after the open PRs land." Now REQUIRED for all hosts and
all repos on all hosts.

  A version exists ONCE per repo. A .csproj names a package; it never names a version.

WHY (measured in GLPNET on 2026-09-01, before this file existed) — three packages
were pinned at TWO different versions simultaneously across the 31 projects:

    xunit                       2.9.2   AND 2.9.3
    Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk      17.11.1 AND 17.14.1
    xunit.runner.visualstudio   2.8.2   AND 3.1.4

Each drift is resolved below to the HIGHER version. A per-project bump would have
fixed those three refs and left the mechanism that produced them intact — which is
precisely the reasoning recorded in the ruling.

🔴 FLOATING VERSIONS ARE BANNED (ruling Q-shiras-36).
Never write `10.*`, `*`, or a `[range]`. A floating `10.*` silently follows the .NET 10
line and WILL NEVER MOVE TO 11 ON ITS OWN — it would quietly defeat the .NET 11
mandate while every scan reported compliance. GLPNET was measured clean of floating
versions at adoption; this comment is the guard that keeps it that way.

  Preconditions verified before adopting, per the ruling's sequencing requirement:
    - open PRs against GLPNET at adoption time: ZERO (`gh pr list`, state=open)
    - floating versions present at adoption time: NONE

HOW TO ADD A PACKAGE
  1. Add a <PackageVersion Include="X" Version="N" /> line here.
  2. In the .csproj write <PackageReference Include="X" /> with NO Version attribute.
-->
<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <!-- A .csproj that still carries a Version= attribute is an ERROR, not a warning:
         a silent override is exactly the drift this file exists to remove. -->
    <CentralPackageVersionOverrideEnabled>false</CentralPackageVersionOverrideEnabled>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Test stack">
    <!-- DRIFT RESOLVED 2026-09-01: was 17.11.1 and 17.14.1 -> 17.14.1 -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.14.1" />
    <!-- DRIFT RESOLVED 2026-09-01: was 2.9.2 and 2.9.3 -> 2.9.3 -->
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit" Version="2.9.3" />
    <!-- DRIFT RESOLVED 2026-09-01: was 2.8.2 and 3.1.4 -> 3.1.4 -->
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="3.1.4" />
    <PackageVersion Include="coverlet.collector" Version="6.0.4" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Runtime and hosting">
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.WindowsServices" Version="9.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Parsing, transport, data">
    <PackageVersion Include="Antlr4.Runtime.Standard" Version="4.13.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="NetMQ" Version="4.0.4.3" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Npgsql" Version="8.0.4" />
    <PackageVersion Include="YamlDotNet" Version="16.2.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Cryptography and encoding">
    <PackageVersion Include="BouncyCastle.Cryptography" Version="2.4.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="NSec.Cryptography" Version="24.4.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="System.Formats.Cbor" Version="9.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
